@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_ics20_trace_escrow|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Identical base denomination text may refer to different vouchers on distinct authenticated transfer paths; source/sink branch confusion can invalidate escrow accounting.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_webhook_durable_effect|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=At-least-once delivery and a crash between separate commits permit duplicate effects or dropped work; timestamps do not establish event ordering.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_redis_lease_not_ledger|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=After expiry a second worker may enter while the paused first worker resumes; an unconditional DEL can release someone else's lease.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_refund_reservation_cas|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Independent check-then-write permits their combined reservations to exceed the captured amount; reusing a key for a different amount aliases different operations.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_solana_independent_account_checks|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=A matching type discriminator does not prove owner, PDA namespace, signer or authority; deriving an address does not create or initialize its account.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_solana_seed_namespace|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Different logical seed tuples can share concatenated bytes; an address valid for a different authority is not authorization for this operation.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_solana_cpi_state_sync|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=CPI inherits granted privileges; cached high-level state can disagree with account bytes changed by CPI. Direct self-recursion and indirect reentrancy have different runtime rules.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_aead_nonce_uniqueness|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Reusing a (key, nonce) pair reproduces the identical keystream mask (C1 XOR C2 == P1 XOR P2) and exposes polynomial MAC evaluation points (GHASH/Poly1305), allowing plaintext recovery and tag forgery.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_flash_accounting_zero_net_delta|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=If intermediate callback frames can mint claimable credit or withdraw funds while net currency delta remains negative, an attacker extracts unbacked value before the outer lock closes.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_crs_archive_path_canonicalization|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Relative parent segments (../) or symlinks inside archive member filenames resolve outside the destination directory, enabling arbitrary file overwrite (Zip Slip / CWE-22) despite a valid outer extension.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=rt_scar_001|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Reading VVS_Rewarder/Contract.sol:793-877 proved Rewarder.UserInfo ONLY stores rewardDebt (never user.amount) and queries craftsmanV2.userInfo(_pid, _user) live. Setting user.amount = 0 in CraftsmanV2 immediately zeroes the user's stake in Rewarder.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=rt_scar_002|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=In CraftsmanV2 (a wrapper around CraftsmanV1), per-pool allocation points and pendingVVS are tracked independently per _pid inside CraftsmanV1, and every deposit/withdraw calls updatePool(_pid) directly. Thus skipping massUpdatePools has zero mathematical effect on rewards or principal.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=rt_scar_003|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=In H2_MasterChefV3, decreaseLiquidity(L456) passes _to = address(0) to harvestOperation (recording rewards in storage without calling h2.safeTransfer), and collect(L473) withdraws 100% of underlying token0/token1 principal and fees without touching h2.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=rt_scar_004|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=pay() (L428-L434) pulls token0 and token1 from msg.sender via safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, ...) after checkpointing the NFT owner's rewards. Calling increaseLiquidity on another user's NFT simply donates the caller's own tokens to the victim.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=rt_scar_005|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Veno_Rewarder.sol:121-131 explicitly documents InconsistentPayout as an intentional optimistic-concurrency guard for the Merkle bot. And x/cronos/keeper/keeper_test.go:176-343 explicitly tests that SetExternalContractForDenom must reject already-mapped denoms to prevent stranding escrowed coins, while GetContractByDenom's fallback is solely for legacy state.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=rt_scar_006|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Live read-only eth_call checks proved: (1) Fulcrom maxLongToShortRatio == 0 across all 3 tokens on Cronos zkEVM (disabled) and decreasing guaranteedUsd makes maxShortToLongRatio stricter, not looser; (2) VenoStorm totalLockShare == 7500 on-chain; (3) LiquidCro treasury (0xc7b8...306d) has eth_getCode == '0x' (an EOA where 2300-gas transfer cannot fail).|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=rt_scar_007|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=BlockAddressesDecorator reads local node CLI flag --halt-blocked-addresses; running a node-local CLI flag inside DeliverTx would cause an immediate consensus state-root fork across nodes. On-chain blocklist enforcement is performed at consensus level in PrepareProposal/ProcessProposal (app/proposal.go:82, 339-354).|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=rt_scar_008|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Tier-2 confirmed three real technical discrepancies (including EthCall/EstimateGas/eth_simulateV1 failing on self-sponsored EIP-7702 auths and cross-message EIP-7702 nonce pre-increment in batched sdk.Tx). However, under R102/R103, neither allows an attacker to unilaterally drain an arbitrary user's principal without the victim signing a future-nonce EIP-7702 delegation alongside an unconfirmed tx.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=rt_scar_009|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Not only are both functions strictly gated by onlyRole(ROLE_BOT) (excluded under R102/R103), TransactionManager.sol:L80,L109 and PerpVaultDeposit.sol:L55 pull 1:1 underlying ybEth/ybUsd tokens directly from msg.sender (ROLE_BOT) via safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, ...). A duplicate _txId cannot mint unbacked tokens.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=rt_scar_010|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=In VVSZap.sol:1115, `if (lastFetchedPairIndex < endAtPairIndex - 1) { lastFetchedPairIndex = endAtPairIndex - 1; }` strictly updates forward only, and passing (0, 0) reverts on `endAtPairIndex - 1` underflow in Solidity ^0.8.0. VVSZap holds zero user principal, and IGOV2 <100 wei revert is sub-dust.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=rt_scar_011|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Inspecting contracts/src/ModuleCRC21.sol and ModuleCRC20.sol proves auto-deployed contracts never define or emit __CronosSendToAccount. Only external contracts registered via CanChangeTokenMapping (CronosAdmin/Gov) can trigger SendToAccountHandler, which calls bankKeeper.SendCoins from the contract's own bank balance (never MintCoins), and sdk.NewCoins strips zero amounts to empty Coins{}.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=rt_scar_012|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Because `updatePidZeroRatio(100)` calls `_updatePidZeroPool()` synchronously inside the same transaction (`src_VenoStorm.sol:L220`), dividing by `100 - 100 == 0` when `points != 0` atomically reverts the owner's own setter call in Solidity 0.8.15—the invalid `pidZeroRatio = 100` state can never be committed to storage.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=rt_scar_013|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=In `src_LiquidCro.sol:L157,L167,L215`, `requestUnbond` decrements `totalPooledCro` by the exact same rounded-down `croAmount` that `unbond` later transfers out. Any truncation is <1e-8 CRO in favor of the pool (never against pool solvency) and matches Crypto.org Chain's 8-decimal `basecro` precision (`MAX_8_DECIMALS`).|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=rt_scar_014|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Root-cause analysis and Council #1 verified that once PULL 1 and PULL 2 notes are filed >=24h apart, CSV bytes must remain 100% immutable, all date-index/change-section tables must be computed programmatically from the exact verified CSV files, and every claim must pass R129 cross-verification.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_c026_t1_veno_l1_01_bridge_zkcro_funding_invariant|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=BridgeMiddleware swaps ETH to zkCRO and stores it; ZkCroMintAndBridge mints zkCRO using CRO, and the bridge calls must conserve the total funded amount.|out=|rule=
