@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=custom_rule_meta-rule-001|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Truy vết luồng xác minh bằng chứng Merkle/ZK liên file; bắt buộc gắn tiền tố phân tách lá/nút trong (0x00/0x01) và khóa cứng (srcChainId, dstChainId, bridgeContract, nonce). [shell_security_recon] rg -n -C 3 '(MerkleProof|verifyProof|keccak256\(abi\.encodePacked)' audits/|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=custom_rule_meta-rule-002|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Kiểm toán các tài khoản Solana/Anchor thiếu ràng buộc owner, signer, canonical bump hoặc ép kiểu u128->u64 tràn số, sử dụng công cụ tĩnh chỉ đọc tuyệt đối không qua shell. [shell_security_recon] rg -n -C 3 '(AccountInfo|invoke_signed|as u64|unchecked_account)' audits/|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=custom_rule_meta-rule-003|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Chống bất đồng bộ phân tích cú pháp giữa Reverse Proxy/WAF và Backend thanh toán; bắt buộc xác thực HMAC trên raw_body nguyên bản và khóa CAS nguyên tử cho webhook. [shell_security_recon] rg -n -C 3 '(compare_digest|webhook|idempoten|Transfer-Encoding)' scripts/ data/local_brain/labs/|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=custom_rule_meta-rule-004|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Kiểm toán lỗi làm tròn số học ERC-4626 (inflation/rounding) và reentrancy; tự động hạ cờ REFUTED_S3_SAFE nếu hàm đã có virtual shares/assets offset, nonReentrant và mulDiv làm tròn có lợi cho Vault. [shell_security_recon] rg -n -C 3 '(convertToShares|convertToAssets|mulDiv|nonReentrant)' audits/|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=custom_rule_meta-rule-005|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Phát hiện lệch trạng thái giữa bộ đệm EVM `StateDB` và `sdk.Context` MultiStore khi hợp đồng gọi vào precompile rồi cố tình `revert` khung gọi con. [shell_security_recon] rg -n -C 3 '(CacheContext|StateDB|Snapshot|readOnly)' audits/|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=custom_rule_meta-rule-006|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Ngăn chặn tấn công nhầm lẫn thuật toán (`alg=none`, RS256 sang HS256), tiêm `jku`/`kid` động, và bắt buộc niêm phong HMAC-SHA256 cho mọi tệp cấu hình/quy tắc. [shell_security_recon] rg -n -C 3 '(jwt\.decode|algorithms=|verify_signature|compare_digest)' scripts/ audits/|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=custom_rule_meta-rule-007|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Chặn SSRF qua chuyển hướng hoặc DNS rebinding về dải nội bộ, chặn đọc tệp vượt thư mục gốc (`realpath`), và khóa cứng `Host`/`Origin` cho dịch vụ cục bộ. [shell_security_recon] rg -n -C 3 '(is_relative_to|realpath|HTTPRedirectHandler|Sec-Fetch-Site)' scripts/ data/local_brain/labs/|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=custom_rule_meta-rule-008|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Phòng thủ tấn công AI Indirect Prompt Injection (IPI) qua ngữ cảnh RAG/tài liệu ngoài, buôn lậu thẻ Unicode ẩn, và đầu độc mô tả JSON Schema hoặc chiếm quyền trùng tên công cụ (Tool Shadowing) giữa các máy chủ MCP. [shell_security_recon] rg -n -C 3 '(source_is_untrusted_rag|duplicate_tool_name_shadowed|schema_description_prompt_injection|policy_gate_allowlist)' data/local_brain/labs/ scripts/|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=custom_rule_meta-rule-009|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Ngăn chặn thực thi mã từ xa (RCE) qua fallback giải tuần tự hóa Pickle khi nạp trọng số mô hình AI, chặn bom JSON header trên SafeTensors/ONNX external_data traversal, và bảo vệ vỏ não tri thức Cortex khỏi các nguyên tử bị đầu độc (Memory Poisoning). [shell_security_recon] rg -n -C 3 '(used_unsafe_pickle_fallback|header_json_size_mb|weights_only|external_data_path_traversal)' data/local_brain/labs/ scripts/|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=custom_rule_meta-rule-010|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Triệt tiêu các biến thể bypass bộ lọc AI do lệch pha chuẩn hóa ký tự (Unicode Tag/Bidi/NFKC), trôi ngữ cảnh đa lượt (Multi-turn Crescendo), hạ cấp model ngầm tại Router (CM-017), và bẫy thao túng phán quyết đơn mô hình (Judge Sycophancy / Canary Honeypot). [shell_security_recon] rg -n -C 3 '(sanitize_external_untrusted_text|_sanitize_and_assert_whitehat_prose|InstantLieDownBrake|require_grok_model)' scripts/|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=custom_rule_meta-rule-011|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Đóng điểm mù khoảng trống ngữ nghĩa – cú pháp khi gọi công cụ AI (JSON hợp lệ nhưng gây tác động nghiệp vụ trái phép), chặn kế thừa nhiễm bẩn qua nhiều lượt chat/cache/job nền (CrossTurnAsyncTaintGraph), và chặn rò rỉ dữ liệu qua ảnh Markdown/link preview ngoại vi. [shell_security_recon] rg -n -C 3 '(SemanticEffectIntentGate|CrossTurnAsyncTaintGraph|ZeroEgressPreviewSideChannelBroker|parse_strict_unique_json)' data/local_brain/labs/ scripts/|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=custom_rule_meta-rule-012|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Triệt tiêu điểm mù đồng thuận giả giữa các họ AI thương mại (Gemini CaMeL, ChatGPT Hierarchy, Grok Circuit-Breaker) do trùng lặp tập huấn luyện mở, ngăn System-2 Z3/AST đóng dấu an toàn trên đặc tả thiếu vế, và khóa đồng nhất SHELL_AUDIT_SANDBOX_PROFILE ở tầng nhân. [shell_security_recon] rg -n -C 3 '(GroundedEvidenceCouncilQuorumGate|FrontierProviderDefenseTriad|SHELL_AUDIT_SANDBOX_PROFILE)' data/local_brain/labs/ scripts/|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=custom_rule_meta-rule-013|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Xác minh họ model thực tế từ gateway (CM-017), lọc tuyến tính cả <think> lẫn <thinking>, chặn tràn reasoning_content vào content, và không nhầm văn bản từ chối <untrusted_doc> với lỗi prompt injection. [shell_security_recon] rg -n -- 'detect_model_identity_spoof|_extract_verified_final_content|_NoRedirectStrict' scripts/free_gateway_client.py|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_aibs_c048_bs1_sema_01_semantic_effect_authorization|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=In data/local_brain/labs/ai_blindspot_and_bypass_defense_arena/arena_01_semantic_and_async_state/app/semantic_async_taint_sink.py, the visible sink rejects invalid schemas and separately checks consequential effects and allowlist membership against owner approval. scripts/harness_atomic_security_core.py documents external-text sanitation, while data/local_brain/labs/frontier_ai_security_gauntlet_v107/frontier_ai_security_gauntlet_lab.py names a namespace-pinning/schema-sanitizer invariant; their actual wiring is not shown.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_aibs_c048_bs1_sema_02_async_taint_provenance_closure|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=The generated-code excerpt in data/local_brain/labs/ai_blindspot_and_bypass_defense_arena/ai_blindspot_defense_lab.py blocks when bond_amt is nonzero, drift exceeds Decimal("0.60"), any_taint is true, or signed_intent_manifest_verified is absent or false. scripts/harness_atomic_security_core.py documents is_strictly_zero_bond as rejecting nonfinite and positive bonds, and the companion sink separately gates consequential effects on owner approval; provenance propagation and their integration remain unshown.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_aibs_c048_bs2_pars_01_canonical_parser_attestation|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=The visible sink blocks when has_duplicate_json_key is truthy or single_parser_verified is absent or false, while canonicalize_single_representation applies NFKC and removes Cf and Unicode tag characters. scripts/harness_atomic_security_core.py separately documents sanitize_external_untrusted_text for external Unicode and indirect-injection handling, but its implementation and integration with this sink are not shown.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_aibs_c048_bs2_pars_02_ocr_taint_authority_quarantine|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=canonical_parser_multimodal_sink.py rejects a truthy unquarantined_ocr_stream with MULTIMODAL_OCR_QUARANTINE_REQUIRED. The generated guard fragment in ai_blindspot_defense_lab.py additionally blocks any_taint or missing signed_intent_manifest_verified and checks owner_explicit_approval for consequential_side_effect, although their execution together is not demonstrated.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_aibs_c048_bs3_tria_01_hierarchy_semantic_sink_binding|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=The visible provider_triad_defense_sink.py slice blocks a truthy lower_ring_hierarchy_override and begins a rejection branch for constrained_output_mode outside ALLOWED_CONSTRAINED_MODES. These checks provide companion boundary checks for the council request path only if callers invoke them with trusted, independently derived state; that integration is not visible.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_aibs_c048_bs3_tria_02_council_usage_reserve_integrity|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=The visible aggregator skips non-dictionaries and converts token fields with int, while the quota guard clamps batch_remaining against both MAX_BATCH_TOKENS and TOTAL_POOL_TOKENS minus OWNER_RESERVE_TOKENS. Together these expose accounting and policy checkpoints, but the excerpts do not show nonnegative validation, atomic reservation, or a fail-closed connection between them.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_aibs_c048_bs4_egrs_01_preview_redirect_egress|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=The shown sink blocks cross_origin_auth_redirect, missing or false sandbox_network_denied, and truthy external_markdown_preview_url before returning its success gate. The companion harness documents sanitize_external_untrusted_text, while the studio documents a Host/Origin/Sec-Fetch-Site fence; these cover separate ingress boundaries and do not themselves prove outbound fetch confinement.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_aibs_c048_bs4_egrs_02_kernel_seatbelt_parity|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=The shown sink rejects truthy thin_seatbelt_allows_users_read and missing or false kernel_seatbelt_denies_users_secrets, after checking egress restrictions. The harness documents symlink-refusing atomic writes, and the self-defense lab names a wallet-and-secret firewall scenario; neither establishes that a kernel Seatbelt profile is installed or inherited.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_aibs_c048_bs5_cncl_01_correlated_quorum_witness|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=The visible sink returns FAIL_CLOSED_COUNCIL_QUORUM when quorum_timeout_fail_open is truthy or distinct_model_families converts to an integer below two. It also shows an ungrounded_council_consensus condition and a CORRELATED_CONSENSUS_BRAKED_NO_WITNESS return, although the intervening predicate is omitted; _aggregate_usage provides accounting, not proof of independence.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_aibs_c048_bs5_cncl_02_heuristic_exclusion_spec_coverage|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=The engine excerpt sets keep_for_system2 to false when transform_grade ends in :S3 and best_overlap is at least 0.75, so the visible heuristic alone does not establish semantic safety. The sink independently blocks a truthy incomplete_z3_spec_gap or a missing or false spec_mutation_survived, but the supplied excerpts do not prove these checks cover candidates excluded by the engine.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_c053_ad2_cosm_a_01_module_receiving_default_deny|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=If a bank transfer path omits its receiving policy, external deposits could violate module accounting assumptions without necessarily changing total supply. BlockedAddrs visibly assigns !allowedReceivingModAcc[acc] for each maccPerms entry, but the supplied companion excerpts do not show a bank enforcement call.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_c053_ad2_cosm_a_02_keeper_authority_identity_binding|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Address syntax validation alone cannot prevent an unrelated valid address from requesting privileged state or asset-mapping changes. NewKeeper rejects an authority rejected by sdk.AccAddressFromBech32, but no privileged message handler or caller comparison is present in the excerpts.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_c053_ad2_cosm_a_03_proposal_fee_context_consistency|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=If a fee consumer combines values from different execution contexts or invokes an uninitialized callback, fee acceptance could diverge from execution and accounting. The visible closure uses the same ctx for both reads and is assigned after keeper creation, while the companion constructor merely stores its injected evmKeeper.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_c053_ad3_jwt_au_01_nonce_consumption_scope|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Nếu một ủy quyền chuyển tài sản có thể được thực hiện nhiều lần, cùng một khoản ủy quyền có thể tạo nhiều lần giải ngân; đưa _saltHex vào thông điệp không tự tiêu thụ salt. Các kiểm thử nonce thể hiện yêu cầu từ chối nonce đã dùng và phân biệt biên từ 255 sang 256, nhưng không chứng minh bridge áp dụng cơ chế đó.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_c053_ad3_jwt_au_02_signature_context_consistency|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Nếu một overload chấp nhận sai signer, sai digest hoặc phản hồi ví không hợp lệ, kẻ không được ủy quyền có thể kích hoạt thay đổi trạng thái tài sản. Các kiểm thử Solidity yêu cầu kết quả false cho signer bằng không, digest sai và ví malicious; các assertion Python hiển thị yêu cầu từ chối trên nhiều biểu diễn chữ ký và đường calldata.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_c053_ad3_jwt_au_03_bridge_signature_domain_binding|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Một chữ ký hợp lệ trên digest vẫn có thể bị dùng sai ngữ cảnh nếu digest không phân biệt các triển khai bridge dùng chung signer, dẫn đến giải ngân ngoài miền dự định. Thông điệp hiển thị đã gắn người gửi, người nhận, token, gas, amount, hai chain ID, deadline và salt, nhưng không hiển thị địa chỉ hợp đồng xác minh; kiểm thử digest sai không thay thế ràng buộc miền.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_c053_ad5_paym_a_01_lease_exclusion_and_submission_check|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=If workers perform the same payable action without a shared lease and durable operation identity, retries can duplicate work or submission attempts. The hub visibly reads job state under hub_lock and rejects specified terminal states and another worker's unexpired lease, but the excerpt does not show lease persistence or server-side settlement deduplication.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_c053_ad5_paym_a_02_canonical_fetch_target_and_evidence_|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=A lexical startswith("http") test does not establish a valid public HTTP(S) destination, so an unguarded downstream fetch could cross network boundaries or produce misleading proof inputs. The survey window records error status and response hashes, but these provenance fields are not destination authorization or successful-content validation.|out=|rule=
@CAUSAL_ATOM/1|id=overnight_grok_c053_ad5_paym_a_03_locked_cohort_and_verified_artifact_|dom=backend|cat=general|conf=0.98|trig=|mech=Replacing a locked cohort with current discovery results can silently change the purchased dataset, while advancing a checkpoint before verifying the uploaded artifact can acknowledge different or missing evidence. The visible merge iterates locked certificate keys and falls back to locked records, and the survey retains body and header references, but neither fragment demonstrates transactional upload-to-checkpoint binding.|out=|rule=

# === SECTION 5: LOCAL EMPIRICAL LESSONS (41) & SWARM MERGED PLAYBOOKS (7) ===
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-API-001|dom=backend-api|title=Never call synchronous time.sleep() inside an async def coroutine|trap=Used `time.sleep(seconds)` for retry backoff inside an `async def` handler thinking it only pauses the current request.|law=Cooperative event loops run on a single OS thread; a synchronous `time.sleep()` freezes every concurrent WebSocket and HTTP request on the worker.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-API-002|dom=backend-api|title=Multi-Tenant Cache & Secondary Query Isolation: Always prefix cache keys with tenant_id|trap=Filtered the primary SQL query by `tenant_id`, but keyed the Redis cache lookup by bare `record_id` (`cache.get(f'record:{record_id}')`), leaking cached records across tenants.|law=Every secondary retrieval path, cache key, and export job must bind the authenticated `tenant_id` (`f'tenant:{tenant_id}:record:{record_id}'`); row-level security on the DB does not protect an unscoped cache hit.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-API-003|dom=backend-api|title=HTTP Redirect Effective-Host Verification & Verbatim Raw-Byte Archival|trap=Treated `resp.status == 200` after redirects as valid full-text retrieval even when redirected to an `/unblock` or captcha interstitial, and re-serialized JSON via `json.dumps(indent=2)` instead of slicing raw bytes.|law=Always verify `urllib.parse.urlparse(resp.geturl()).hostname == expected_host`, send `Cache-Control: no-cache`, and archive/slice the verbatim `raw_bytes` before parsing.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-BIZ-001|dom=business-negotiation|title=Anti-Scope-Creep Gate: Bind every out-of-scope client request to a written change order and fee/timeline delta|trap=Said 'Sure, we can throw in that extra module for free' to please a client during delivery, eroding project margin and delaying core milestones.|law=Unpriced concessions train clients that your time has zero marginal cost. Always welcome new ideas warmly while anchoring them to a formal Change Order (`CHANGE_ORDER_WITH_FEE_AND_TIMELINE`).
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-BIZ-002|dom=business-negotiation|title=Never volunteer a unilateral price discount before establishing ROI and receiving a concrete counter-commitment|trap=Offered an immediate 40% discount in the first outreach message out of fear that the prospect might find the full price too high.|law=Pre-emptive discounting signals low confidence in product value. Anchor on quantified ROI first; if trading price down, always extract a concrete quid-pro-quo (annual prepay, case study, or volume commitment).
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-CAP-001|dom=finance-capital|title=Zero-Advance-Fee Capital Guard: Reject any contract or opportunity requiring an upfront verification deposit|trap=Felt tempted by a high promised payout (`$500 return`) to pay a 'small refundable verification deposit or staking fee' (`upfront_fee_usd > 0`).|law=Legitimate commercial counterparties deduct service fees from gross settlements or pay inbound; any requirement to send upfront principal (`UPFRONT_DEPOSIT_REQUIRED` / `upfront_fee_usd > 0`) is an asymmetric principal-loss trap.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-CAP-002|dom=finance-capital|title=Anti-Martingale Position Sizing: Never double exposure after a losing trade or drawdown|trap=Doubled position size after a loss (`next_bet = last_bet * 2`) to 'win back losses in one trade' due to loss-aversion panic.|law=Volatility clusters in real life and markets; Martingale doubling (`MARTINGALE_DOUBLE_DOWN`) guarantees ruin under finite capital. Cap every single-decision risk to <= 1%–2% of liquid net worth.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-DEC-001|dom=decision-strategy|title=One-Way Door Pre-Mortem Gate: Require explicit downside bounds and kill-criteria before irreversible decisions|trap=Treated an irreversible Type-1 ('One-Way Door') commitment with the same casual speed as a reversible Type-2 experiment, without defining a pre-mortem or exit trigger.|law=Harvested from anthropics/skills (discernment-nudge): Before executing any irreversible decision, explicitly write down the worst-case downside, key unverified assumptions, and concrete kill-criteria.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-DEC-002|dom=decision-strategy|title=Anti-Over-Engineering Gate: Reject speculative abstractions, kitchen-sink wrappers, and unrequested features|trap=Built an abstract 5-layer factory framework and 12 speculative config flags for a problem that only needed one deterministic 20-line function.|law=Harvested from patrickjs/awesome-cursorrules (anti-overengineering): Complexity is a permanent maintenance tax. Solve only what was asked with the simplest deterministic mechanism first.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-EPI-001|dom=research-epistemology|title=Anti-Sycophancy & Primary-Source Epistemology: Verify primary data before agreeing with user premises|trap=Agreed immediately with a flawed user assumption ('You are absolutely right!') or cited a secondary rumor without checking the primary empirical source.|law=Harvested from patrickjs/awesome-cursorrules (anti-sycophancy-code-discipline): Truth outranks politeness. Verify primary artifacts, measurements, and source code before endorsing any claim.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-EPI-002|dom=research-epistemology|title=Symplectic Hamiltonian Integration & 1st Law Energy Conservation Guard|trap=Integrated a conservative Hamiltonian/orbital system with explicit Forward Euler (`x_next = x_pos + v_vel * dt_sec`), whose Jacobian determinant `det(J) = 1 + omega^2 * dt^2 > 1` pumps artificial energy into the system over long horizons.|law=First Law of Thermodynamics & Liouville's Theorem: Conservative dynamical systems must use a symplectic integrator (Velocity-Verlet / Leapfrog `v_half`) and verify bounded Hamiltonian energy `|E(t) - E(0)| <= tol`.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-EPI-003|dom=research-epistemology|title=Buckingham Pi Dimensional Homogeneity, Radian Conversion & Mass Continuity Guard|trap=Added quantities with incompatible SI dimensions (`pressure_pa + velocity_ms + elevation_mm`), passed degree angles directly into `math.sin(tilt_deg)`, or updated compartment density without antisymmetric mass balance (`rho < 0`).|law=Buckingham Pi & Continuity (`d_rho/dt + div(rho*u) = 0`): Normalize all additive terms to identical SI base units, convert degrees via `math.radians()`, and enforce antisymmetric positivity-preserving mass fluxes.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-FE-001|dom=frontend-ts|title=Wait for networkidle or explicit DOM readiness before inspecting dynamic web apps in Playwright|trap=Inspected DOM elements immediately after `page.goto()` or used arbitrary fixed `page.wait_for_timeout(5000)` before client-side hydration finished.|law=Harvested from anthropics/skills (webapp-testing): Modern SPAs hydrate asynchronously; always wait for `page.wait_for_load_state('networkidle')` or deterministic locator visibility rather than arbitrary blind sleeps.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-FIN-001|dom=fintech-web3|title=Use constant-time hmac.compare_digest() for webhook and payment signatures|trap=Compared `webhook_signature == expected_hmac_digest` using standard string equality `==`.|law=Standard `==` short-circuits on the first mismatched byte, leaking signature bytes via microsecond timing side channels; always use `hmac.compare_digest`.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-FIN-002|dom=fintech-web3|title=Never hardcode calculated sum/margin totals into financial spreadsheet cells; emit live Excel formulas|trap=Computed `total = sum(rows)` in Python and wrote the static float `ws['B10'] = 48500.0` into the `.xlsx` cell, breaking spreadsheet recalculation when inputs change.|law=Harvested from anthropics/skills (xlsx): Financial workbooks must remain dynamically auditable; write live Excel formulas (`=SUM(B2:B9)`) for all subtotal, tax, and margin cells.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-FIN-003|dom=fintech-web3|title=Atomic Ledger Locking (TOCTOU) & Symmetric Decimal Scaling Guard|trap=Checked account balance at t1 (`SELECT balance`) and deducted at t2 without row-level locking or atomic conditional debit, while rounding 18-decimal internal units down on debit and up on 6-decimal payout.|law=Concurrent withdrawals race between unlocked reads and writes (`TOCTOU_UNLOCKED_LEDGER_DEBIT`). Enforce atomic `UPDATE ... WHERE balance >= amount` (or `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`) and use identical floor-quantized atomic units for both debit and payout.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-FIN-004|dom=fintech-web3|title=Bind cryptographic signatures to (chainId, verifyingContract, nonce, deadline) and update vault shares before external calls|trap=Verified a withdrawal signature without binding `(chainId, verifyingContract, nonce, deadline)` and transferred vault assets before burning shares, exposing mid-callback share price skew.|law=Unscoped signatures enable cross-context replay, and transferring assets before burning shares creates a read-only reentrancy window where `totalAssets / totalSupply` is artificially depressed.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-FIN-005|dom=fintech-web3|title=Deterministic Wallet Derivation & Closed-Loop Sign-Recover Gate|trap=Added an `except ImportError:` fallback that generated random hex bytes when `eth_account` was missing in a virtualenv, creating unbacked payout addresses with no matching private key.|law=Never fallback to random bytes when deriving cryptographic addresses; fail hard if signing libraries are missing and require a closed-loop `recover(sign(msg, pk)) == address` assertion before registering any payout address.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-GRW-001|dom=growth-marketing|title=Organic Trust Warmup (95/5 Rule): Never blast outbound promo links from fresh or low-karma community accounts|trap=Posted external promotional URLs on day 1 from a brand-new account (`account_age_days < 7`), triggering automated anti-spam filters and permanent domain shadowbans.|law=Communities reward native problem-solving and penalize extraction. Follow the 95/5 rule: deliver 95% zero-link domain value until trust/karma matures, then introduce relevant resources naturally.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-HIGH-001|dom=ai-agents-mcp|title=No Unsupported Promotion Across Scopes or Evidence Types (Lakatosian CEGIS, 4-State Symbolic Path & Brier Second-Moment Guard)|trap=Upgraded a domain-cut CONDITIONAL claim, an timed-out SURRENDER refutation, an UNKNOWN interval enclosure, a confounded regression, or an empirical ensemble vote (`EMPIRICAL_CONFIDENCE`) into a universal `PROVED` certificate.|law=Carry `(claim_id, scope, assumptions, evidence_lineage, status)` on every output: enforce Lakatosian anti-goalpost-moving (`CONDITIONAL` on domain cuts, `SURRENDER` on incomplete refuter), 4-state outward-rounded symbolic path evaluation (`UNREACHABLE`/`HOLDS`/`VIOLATED`/`UNKNOWN`), moralized ancestral d-separation, and uncentered Brier second-moment shrinkage (`w^T E[e e^T] w`).
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-HLT-001|dom=health-longevity|title=Circadian & Cognitive Recovery Guard: Block late caffeine and连续 >4h unpaused deep-work marathons|trap=Drank espresso at 19:00 and coded for 6 hours straight without standing up, mistaking acute adrenaline stimulation for sustainable productivity.|law=Caffeine has a ~5–6h half-life that fragments slow-wave and REM sleep, compounding next-day cognitive error rates by >40%. Protect the 8-hour pre-sleep caffeine cutoff and 90-minute ultradian breaks.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-LEG-001|dom=legal-contracts|title=Contract Liability Cap: Never sign agreements with uncapped consequential damages or unilateral indemnity|trap=Signed a standard enterprise vendor MSA without checking the limitation of liability clause, exposing personal or company assets to unlimited consequential damages.|law=Every commercial contract must cap aggregate liability to a deterministic multiple of fees actually paid (typically 12 months of fees) and exclude indirect/consequential damages.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-LEG-002|dom=legal-contracts|title=Background IP Retention: Carve out pre-existing tools, frameworks, and harnesses from client IP assignment clauses|trap=Signed a work-for-hire agreement assigning 'all tools, scripts, and know-how used during the engagement', accidentally transferring ownership of your proprietary harness.|law=Always separate Background IP (your reusable engines, libraries, and methodologies) from Foreground Deliverables: retain 100% ownership of Background IP and grant the client a non-exclusive license.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-MCP-001|dom=ai-agents-mcp|title=Strip bidirectional Unicode overrides in MCP tool inputs and prompts (CVE-2021-42574)|trap=Assumed visually inspected strings in MCP tool arguments or skill files match the byte stream interpreted by the LLM and runtime.|law=Invisible Unicode Bidi overrides (U+202A..U+202E, U+2066..U+2069) invert token order visually while executing hidden directives; reject them at the ingestion boundary.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-MCP-002|dom=ai-agents-mcp|title=Enforce hard iteration and token ceilings on autonomous agent tool loops|trap=Wrote `while True:` around an LLM tool-calling loop assuming the model will always emit a final stop token.|law=When an upstream tool returns a transient error, LLMs frequently enter infinite retry oscillations; every agent loop must be bounded by `range(MAX_STEPS)`.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-MCP-003|dom=ai-agents-mcp|title=Return structured isError=True MCP tool responses instead of raising raw unhandled exceptions|trap=Raised raw unhandled runtime exceptions inside an MCP tool handler assuming the host client will format them into actionable guidance for the LLM.|law=Harvested from anthropics/skills (mcp-builder): MCP tools must return structured `isError: True` payloads with actionable recovery hints so the calling agent can self-correct without crashing the transport.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-MCP-004|dom=ai-agents-mcp|title=Enable prompt caching (cache_control ephemeral) on static system instructions and tool catalogs|trap=Sent the full 20,000-token system prompt and MCP tool schema un-cached on every multi-turn agent step, paying 10x input token costs.|law=Harvested from anthropics/skills (claude-api): Mark static system prompts and tool definitions with `cache_control: {'type': 'ephemeral'}` to cut repeated input token latency and cost by up to 90%.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-MCP-005|dom=ai-agents-mcp|title=Anti-Silent-Model-Downgrade Gate: Verify upstream routed model identity instead of masking with fallback|trap=Wrote `model_used = data.get('model') or requested_model`, silently attributing a low-tier 20B/mini fallback response to a requested Frontier reasoning model.|law=Proxy gateways frequently substitute cheaper models under load; explicitly verify that `data.get('model')` is present and matches the requested Frontier family before trusting high-stakes reasoning output.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-MCP-006|dom=ai-agents-mcp|title=Shadow-Clone Parallel Epistemic Swarm & BFT Synaptic Merge (K=3f+1 Quorum)|trap=Allowed parallel subagents to share intermediate drafts before independent grounding or accepted a single unverified subagent conclusion without a Byzantine-tolerant quorum (`s_p >= 3` of `K=4`).|law=Enforce orthogonal clone tracks with zero inter-clone communication during exploration, ground every clone proposition via the <5ms 3-State Gate + Counterfactual Sandbox, quarantine refuted traps into a Negative Tabu List, and merge only propositions achieving `s_p >= 3` quorum (`K=3f+1`).
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-MCP-007|dom=ai-agents-mcp|title=Covariance-Aware Equicorrelation BFT Merge (N_eff), Disjoint Scar Holdout & Alpha-Normalized AST Quotient|trap=Treated K correlated subagent votes from identical model families as independent (`N_eff = K`), verified synthesized regex scars using the same generator tier without a disjoint paraphrase-mutated negative holdout (`T_gen == T_ver`), or hashed raw AST identifier strings that break under alpha-renaming.|law=Discount correlated votes via Equicorrelation Inverse Log-Odds (`N_eff = K / (1 + (K - 1) * rho_hat)`), enforce `DisjointScarHoldoutVerifier` (`T_gen != T_ver`, `precision >= 0.95`, `0` paraphrase FPs), and verify semantic equivalence via alpha-normalized De Bruijn AST quotient hashes.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-ML-002|dom=data-ml|title=Block look-ahead bias (.shift(-1)) inside feature engineering columns|trap=Used `df['close'].shift(-1)` when constructing an alpha feature column, inadvertently leaking tomorrow's price into today's prediction.|law=Harvested from patrickjs/awesome-cursorrules (alpha-skills-quant-factor-research): Feature matrices X_t must strictly use lagging data (.shift(1) or rolling past windows); negative shifts belong exclusively in label targets Y_t.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-ML-003|dom=data-ml|title=Causal Light-Cone Non-Lookahead, 2nd Law Entropy & Compensated Floating-Point Guard|trap=Accessed future time index `signal_series[idx_t + 1]` at step `idx_t` (violating relativistic causal arrow `t_cause <= t_effect`), decreased isolated entropy, or evaluated `gamma ** 2 - 1.0` at `v << c`.|law=Enforce strict past-only causal masks (`indices <= idx_t`), non-negative isolated entropy production (`dS >= 0`), algebraic factorization (`v_sq / (1.0 - v_sq)`), and Kahan `math.fsum()`.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-OPS-001|dom=devops-cloud|title=Enforce SSH StrictHostKeyChecking=yes in automated deployment pipelines|trap=Passed `-o StrictHostKeyChecking=no` in CI/CD scripts to suppress interactive host key prompts on first connect.|law=Disabling host key verification surrenders SSH authentication to active network MITM interception; pre-populate `known_hosts` and enforce `StrictHostKeyChecking=yes`.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-OPS-002|dom=devops-cloud|title=Singleton Daemon Flock & Event-Driven Wakeup: Never run unlocked overlapping daemons or busy-poll loops|trap=Spawned multiple cron/CLI worker instances without an exclusive file lock (`fcntl.flock`) and busy-polled task status in a tight loop, causing duplicate executions and resource waste.|law=Acquire a non-blocking exclusive lock (`fcntl.flock(lock_fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)`) at daemon startup and yield to event-driven reactive wakeup instead of polling.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-OPS-003|dom=devops-cloud|title=Complete Browser Origin Storage Teardown (IndexedDB + ServiceWorkers) & Scoped Profile Cleanup|trap=Cleared browser cookies when switching accounts (`Network.clearBrowserCookies`) while leaving stale IndexedDB cryptographic keys (`cvm_chip_pin_unavailable`), or ran an unscoped global browser process kill.|law=Navigate to `about:blank` and call `Storage.clearDataForOrigin` for `indexeddb,local_storage,cache_storage,service_workers` before clearing cookies, and terminate only the isolated `--user-data-dir` in `finally`.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-PSY-001|dom=psychology-relationships|title=Emotional Calibration & Anti-Chasing: Never send needy double/triple follow-ups when counterpart investment drops|trap=Felt anxious when a romantic interest or high-value contact took hours to reply, sending multiple needy check-in texts ('Why are you ignoring me???').|law=Attraction and respect require balanced investment velocity (`ping-pong reciprocity`). Chasing silence with needy pressure destroys perceived status; mirror their pace and stay grounded in your own mission.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-PSY-002|dom=psychology-relationships|title=Conflict De-escalation: Enforce a cool-down pause and replace 'You always/never' accusations with factual observations|trap=Replied immediately while angry using absolute character attacks ('You always ruin everything'), triggering amygdala defensiveness in the other person.|law=During emotional spikes, prefrontal reasoning is offline. Enforce a mandatory cool-down interval and frame feedback around specific observable events and shared solutions.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-SEC-001|dom=data-ml|title=Require weights_only=True in PyTorch torch.load() to block pickle RCE|trap=Treated `.pt` / `.bin` model checkpoints as passive weight tensors rather than executable Python pickle bytecode.|law=Default `torch.load()` invokes `pickle.Unpickler`, allowing arbitrary OS command execution during checkpoint deserialization unless `weights_only=True` is set.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-ZTR-001|dom=security-zerotrust|title=Reject JWT verification calls that disable signature checking or allow alg='none'|trap=Set `verify_signature: False` during local debugging to inspect JWT claims and left the option in the authentication middleware.|law=Disabling JWT signature verification or permitting `alg='none'` allows any caller to forge arbitrary admin identities; always pin explicit asymmetric algorithms and verify signatures.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-ZTR-002|dom=security-zerotrust|title=Cross-Layer Path Seam Containment: Never concatenate unvalidated user filenames into open()|trap=Assumed a surface string filter on a user filename prevents directory traversal when concatenated via `open(base_dir + '/' + filename)`.|law=Surface string filters fail against encoding/traversal seams across layers; resolve the canonical path via `Path(base_dir).joinpath(filename).resolve()` and enforce `.is_relative_to(base_root)` before opening.
@EMPIRICAL_LESSON/1|id=KL-ZTR-003|dom=security-zerotrust|title=Anti-Mass-Assignment Privilege Boundary: Never merge raw request dicts into user/account records|trap=Merged parsed HTTP body parameters directly into the stored user model (`user_record.update(request_json)`), allowing callers to inject `is_admin=True` or `balance=999999`.|law=Privilege flags (`is_admin`, `role`, `balance`, `tenant_id`) must never share a merge dictionary with user-editable profile fields; project input through an explicit field allowlist.
